---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Aside from "../components/Aside.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy & Local Files: How Paperling Works"
  description="Understand Paperling's local files, optional AI connections, remote content, update checks, and GitHub Pages hosting."
  path="privacy/"
  crumbs={[{ label: "Privacy & your files", path: "privacy/" }]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR FILES. CLEAR EXPECTATIONS.</p>
      <h1>
        Local by nature.
        <br />
        <em>Clear about connections.</em>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Paperling is a local Markdown editor. That describes where you write and
        save; it does not mean every feature is unable to use the network.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-layout">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Your documents</h2>
        <p>
          Reading and editing local Markdown files work offline. Paperling does
          not require an account or provide a hosted note-sync service. You
          choose the folders, backups, and external storage tools you use.
        </p>
        <h2>Optional AI</h2>
        <p>
          If you configure a remote AI endpoint, that provider receives the
          document context and prompts you send. Its data practices and charges
          apply. A compatible local model server is another option, with its own
          setup requirements. Keep credentials private and avoid including them
          in bug reports.
        </p>
        <h2>Other network activity</h2>
        <p>
          Update checks and downloads connect to the release service. Remote
          images or other online content referenced by a document may contact
          their host. Following external links opens the destination site under
          its own privacy practices.
        </p>
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. It does not add advertising
          trackers or an analytics script. Fonts and artwork are served with the
          site. GitHub can process request information as the hosting provider;
          see its{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
            privacy statement
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <h2>Check the implementation</h2>
        <p>
          Paperling is open source. You can inspect the{" "}
          <a href={SITE.repo}>repository</a> or{" "}
          <a href={SITE.repo + "/issues"}>report a problem</a>. Remove private
          notes, tokens, and API keys before posting publicly.
        </p>
      </article>
      <Aside />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
